The files in this directory are copied from the upstream `automerge` C test
suite, `rust/automerge-c/test/` at commit
`ddbff535407e4d28cd2a82eaf6c6add08caa3bdd`, with one omission, recorded
below. They are MIT-licensed, and that notice is carried here as `AGENTS.md`'s
"Do not copy upstream code into this repository without carrying its licence"
requires.

The one omission: `main.c` is not here. `test/c/main.c` is it, with two
changes and no others — the function is named `suite_main` rather than
`main`, because Zig 0.16's build system cannot use a C file as the root of an
executable and so `test/c/main.zig` has to own `main`; and the sum in it has
one extra term, `run_abi_coverage_tests()`, which is this port's own group in
`test/c/abi_coverage.c`. That group exists because `rust/automerge-c/test/`
calls 147 of the 187 functions `include/automerge.h` declares; without it the
other forty would be linked into the test binary and never executed, which is
exactly what an unrun export looks like. Every other file in this directory
is byte-for-byte upstream, so a `diff -r` against the upstream directory
reports only that `main.c` is missing.

`files/brave-ape-49.automerge` is a test input document from the same
directory and is likewise covered.

